course: dictionary
lesson: 728
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one fits. Read the words around it first. «Mount Everest is the highest mountain above sea level; Mauna Kea, a volcano in Hawaii, is taller measured from its base on the sea floor.» Here base is the bottom part of the mountain, where it starts.
explain: Base has many meanings. It can be a main place where people live or work from, like an army base. In a game of rounders or tag, a base is a safe spot or a place a runner must reach. In maths, the base of a shape is the side it sits on.
explain: To base something on another thing means to use it as a starting point. «Peppa's friends are cartoon animals that talk and go to school, but each one is based on a real animal with its own clever tricks.» Based means the animal's idea started with a real animal. Always test your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Base can be a noun, a verb, or an adjective.
fact: The base of something is its bottom part or the part it stands on.
fact: In maths, a number system has a base, like base ten. In 10 squared, 10 is the base.
fact: In science, a base is a chemical that is the opposite of an acid, like soap or baking soda.
fact: «Tall things stay up when they are stable: a wide base and most of the weight low down make them hard to tip over.»
exercise: In «carved on the base», from the Olympic Games sentence, what does base mean? | A number system like base ten | A safe spot in a game | *The bottom part the statue stands on | A chemical that is the opposite of an acid
exercise: In «measured from its base on the sea floor», what does base mean? | The highest point of a mountain | *The bottom part, where something starts | A main camp for climbers | A safe place to rest
exercise: «Peppa's friends are cartoon animals, but each one is based on a real animal.» What does based mean here? | Hidden away from | Shaped into a ball | Painted to look like | *Took its idea from, as a starting point
test: In a game of rounders, what is a base? | A number in maths | The bottom of a bat | A kind of weather | *A place a runner must reach
test: In science, what is a base? | A type of sugar | A kind of rock | A sour liquid like lemon juice | *A chemical that is the opposite of an acid, like soap
exam: «Tall things stay up when they are stable: a wide base and most of the weight low down make them hard to tip over.» In this sentence, base means what? | To use something as a starting point | A chemical like soap | A main place where people work from | *The bottom part that a tall thing stands on
